<!-- THE LAUNCHER ICON (the manifest's android:icon; the launcher and the
     recents card). Its picture (architect 2026-11-21, send HH): PAPIRUS'S
     NOTE, assets/icons/MusicNote16th.svg, the drawing the app paints in its
     title bar, on the BPM key and on the BPM form's rows
     (assets/icons/README.md its provenance), a
     `currentColor` drawing on a 16 x 16 box (width and height, no viewBox),
     rendered by resvg at the art's height in the
     font color #D3DAE3 (apk/build_apk.sh's LAUNCHER_INK, given as resvg's
     user stylesheet) and centered over THE APP'S GROUND, FLAT: #2F343F
     (architect 2026-11-02: the icon wears the window's own ground;
     Arc-Dark's since 2026-11-18, send Y, the one look since 2026-11-21,
     send GG; both READ by apk/build_apk.sh from the compiled row of the
     look's tones, kArcDarkTones in src/gui/gui_theme.h, its `.ground` and
     `.text` lines, that row the one owner),
     one color over the whole
     canvas, so the mask shows a dark shape carrying the note. An
     ADAPTIVE icon, the whole of it: minSdk is 30, so
     no legacy ic_launcher.png set exists beside it.

     Two layers per density under res/mipmap-<density>/, BOTH RENDERED AT
     EVERY BUILD by apk/build_apk.sh's launcher step into its staged
     copy of res/:
       ic_launcher_background.png  the full 108 dp canvas flat in #2F343F;
       ic_launcher_foreground.png  the drawing rendered 46 dp tall, its width
                                   the box's (46 dp: the note's box is
                                   square; resvg scales the whole 16 x 16
                                   box to the height), centered on a
                                   transparent canvas of the density's full
                                   108 dp.

     THE ART 46 dp (architect 2026-11-22, send II: "take the launcher's icon
     size down a little, leaving it just slightly larger than the old breeze
     version"): the note's 16-unit box at 46 / 16 = 2.875 dp a unit. Its ink
     spans x 4 .. 12 and y 1 .. 15 units (measured off the path data: the
     stem x 8 .. 10, the flag to x 12 over y 1 .. 5, the head a circle of
     radius 3 at (7, 12)), 23 x 40.25 dp — about the width of the Breeze
     note the launcher wore until 2026-11-21 (23.6 x 37.8 dp of ink at its
     52 dp art) and some 6 % taller.

     THE 66 dp SAFE ZONE: an adaptive foreground's art should sit inside the
     mask's guaranteed-visible inner circle, Android's own 66 dp of the 108 dp
     canvas. The note's farthest ink (the flag's top right corner, (12, 1))
     lies sqrt(65) = 8.06 units, 23.2 dp, from the box's center (8, 8),
     inside the 33 dp circle with about 9.8 dp to spare. The same 46 dp at
     every density (the per-density PNG pixel size scales with the density
     factor f alone):

       density  f    canvas C=108f  art 46f  offset (C-46f)/2
       mdpi     1    108            46       31
       hdpi     1.5  162            69       46.5 (magick's center takes
                                                 a whole px, 46)
       xhdpi    2    216            92       62
       xxhdpi   3    324            138      93
       xxxhdpi  4    432            184      124

     A BUILD PRODUCT, NEVER COMMITTED: this file is the one tracked file of
     res/, and build_apk.sh writes the PNGs beside it in the package tree
     (byte-stable, -strip) from assets/icons/MusicNote16th.svg, Papirus's
     note, at the build. The safe-zone figure above is the note's. -->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
</adaptive-icon>
